%N A398996 The binomial matrix of the Motzkin numbers. Square array read by ascending antidiagonals.
%C A398996 See the comments and links in A399000.
%H A398996 Peter Luschny, <a href="https://github.com/PeterLuschny/Gists/blob/main/GnomonicExpansionAndBinomialMatrices.ipynb">Gnomonic Expansion and Binomial Matrices</a>, a Python notebook.
%F A398996 A(n, n) = M(n), the Motzkin numbers.
%F A398996 A(n, k) = Sum_{m=0..d} binomial(d, m) * s^(d - m) * M(p + m), where d = abs(n - k), p = min(n, k), s = 1 if k <= n, otherwise -1.
%e A398996 Array starts:
%e A398996   [0]    1,    0,    1,    0,    2,   0,   5,   0, ...
%e A398996   [1]    2,    1,    1,    1,    2,   2,   5,   5, ...
%e A398996   [2]    5,    3,    2,    2,    3,   4,   7,  10, ...
%e A398996   [3]   14,    9,    6,    4,    5,   7,  11,  17, ...
